hi everyone I'm Tony rich and I'm the  executive director here at the st. Louis  chess club we are really excited that we  can officially open the Chess Club  again this Monday June 22nd so we've  implemented lots of important health and  safety measures to make sure everyone  enjoys their time here while staying  safe six feet apart make sure everybody  stays six feet apart social distancing  is very important we also have these  preventative barriers up that you see  behind me for whenever people are  playing across the board members are  also going to be required to wear masks  asked to wear gloves answer a health  screening question when they come in to  make sure that they haven't been exposed  to kovat in addition to that we ask that  anyone who wants to come in and hang out  here at the Chess Club and play to  register to do so so we'll have two hour  blocks where members can come in play  chess against one another and in between  we're gonna disinfect and clean up  everything and make sure that it's safe  again for the next group of people for  more information about what we're doing  here at the club to keep you safe and to  be able to come back and play some chess  check out st. Louis chess club org or  give us a call at three one four three  six one chess
 

